-- Consolidated baseline schema.
--
-- This replaces 262 incremental migrations (80,641 lines) that had accumulated
-- 4,195 ALTER TABLE statements and 605 ADD COLUMNs — 84 of those files did
-- nothing but alter what earlier ones had built. Reading the schema meant
-- replaying three hundred files in your head, and a version mismatch in the
-- middle of that chain took the whole backend down (VersionMismatch(143)).
--
-- Generated by pg_dump from a database built by applying all 262 in order, so
-- it is the schema that was actually running rather than a hand-rewrite of it.
-- The equivalence was verified by diffing a database built from this file
-- against one built from the 262 — see scripts/verify_baseline.sh.
--
-- The originals are kept under migrations/archive/ rather than deleted: they
-- are the only record of *why* several columns exist.
--
-- psql meta-commands are stripped. PostgreSQL 18's pg_dump emits \restrict,
-- which psql understands and sqlx — sending SQL straight to the server — does
-- not.

